#   What LF and CRLF mean (human version)

#  Text files have invisible “end of line” characters.

#  LF (\n)
#  Used by Linux & macOS

#  CRLF (\r\n)
#  Used by Windows

#  Your warning says:

#  “This file currently uses LF, but Git is going to convert it to CRLF next time it touches it.”

#  That’s it. Nothing more dramatic.